cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the NASA battery dataset it is built on."
type: software
title: "battery-soh: leakage-free Li-ion state-of-health estimation"
abstract: >-
  Estimates the state of health (SOH) of lithium-ion cells from partial-window health
  indicators (a partial constant-current charge, a partial discharge window or EIS),
  never from capacity or any full-discharge statistic. Models are evaluated with
  leave-one-battery-out cross-validation on the NASA PCoE battery dataset, report
  battery-level conformal prediction intervals, and are served by a FastAPI service
  with a static web UI. The project also reproduces and documents the target leakage
  of an earlier version that used capacity as a model input.
authors:
  - given-names: Preran Sai
    family-names: Yarramasu
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - lithium-ion battery
  - state of health
  - prognostics and health management
  - machine learning
  - data leakage
  - conformal prediction
  - leave-one-battery-out
